    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0230" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg134"/>

                <head>No. 82.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Low to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25, 1872</date>.
                        (Received May 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 142.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Since closing my No. 138, of the 15th
                    instant, in which yon were informed of the Emperor’s proposed marriage in
                    October next, several additional decrees concerning the same subject have been
                    issued.</p>
                <p>From them I learn that the 16th of October is the day fixed upon for the
                    marriage; that the betrothal presents are to be bestowed on the 30th of August,
                    and the wedding presents on the 19th of September. In return for the favors
                    granted to him the Emperor has, by decree, conferred additional laudatory titles
                    upon the Empresses. It is also expected that, in accordance with
                    long-established custom and precedent, there will be a special dispensation of
                    imperial bounty, in the form of brevet rank and titles to officials, and several
                    months’ extra pay to the soldiers, when the marriage takes place.</p>
                <p>The belief is becoming general that the marriage of the Emperor and his accession
                    to the throne as sovereign <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> will be
                    simultaneous.</p>
                <p>So strong is this belief that I have reason to think that some of the foreign
                    representatives have already sent telegrams to their governments stating this
                    fact and asking for instructions in regard to making a demand for audience.</p>
                <p>* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have. &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK F. LOW.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
